+          <message name="IDS_SIGNIN_DICE_WEB_INTERCEPT_BUBBLE_CHROME_SIGNIN_IPH_OK_BUTTON" desc="This button appears on a confirmation message, which is intended to help users understand that they have been signed in to Redrob. The user previously signed in to a Google service (like Gmail or Maps), and saw the Redrob Signin Bubble intercept; when asked whether the user wanted to sign in to Redrob as well, the user selected yes. Now, this confirmation appears at the top right of Redrob (pointing at the Profile Menu) to confirm that their choice was effective. This button string comes after the 'Welcome, Elisa' and 'When you sign in on this device, you get your passwords and more from your Google Account' strings. Users click 'Got it' to convey that they saw the message and want to hide the message.">
             Got It
